{"step_index":63,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T14:48:23Z","thinking":"**Exploring radius upper bound**\n\nFor $\\gamma_R \\le 5$, the radius is at most 4. Now, considering $\\gamma_R \\le 6$, a radius of 6 or greater is being investigated. If $\\gamma_R \\le 6$, then $2|Y| + |V \\setminus N[Y]| \\le 6$ for some $Y$. Considering the cases when $|Y| \\le 1$, the eccentricity is $\\le 5$ and hence the radius is $\\le 5$.\nWhen $|Y|=2$,  $|V \\setminus N[Y]| \\le 2$ .\n\n\n**Bounding graph radius with domination**\n\nConsidering the case of two dominating vertices and two exceptional vertices leads to a radius of at most 5.  When the dominating set size is 3, it is a dominating set. This implies that the eccentricity of any vertex $y_i$ is at most 4, making the radius 4. This is based on examining the connectivity of three potentially overlapping neighborhoods.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"python3 -c '\nimport random\nimport itertools\n\ndef fast_roman_tree(n, adj):\n    pass # we already have solve_roman_tree\n\ndef get_radius_and_diam(n, adj):\n    ecc = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        d = [-1]*n\n        d[i] = 0\n        q = [i]\n        for u in q:\n            for v in adj[u]:\n                if d[v] == -1:\n                    d[v] = d[u] + 1\n                    q.append(v)\n        if any(x == -1 for x in d): return None, None\n        ecc.append(max(d))\n    return min(ecc), max(ecc)\n\n# Let us test various graph families:\n# 1. Cycles C_n\n# 2. Paths P_n\n# 3. Grids P_a x P_b\n# 4. Prisms C_a x K_2\n# 5. Mobius ladders\n# 6. Generalized Petersen P(n, k)\n# 7. Circulant graphs\n\ndef fast_roman_subsets(n, adj):\n    mask = [0]*n\n    for i in range(n):\n        m = 1 << i\n        for j in adj[i]: m |= (1 << j)\n        mask[i] = m\n    best = n\n    for size in range(1, (best // 2) + 1):\n        for Y in itertools.combinations(range(n), size):\n            cov = 0\n            for y in Y: cov |= mask[y]\n            w = 2 * size + n - bin(cov).count(\"1\")\n            if w < best:\n                best = w\n    return best\n\nprint(\"Testing named graphs...\")\n# Generalized Petersen\nfor n in range(3, 11):\n    for k in range(1, (n-1)//2 + 1):\n        # 2n vertices\n        adj = [[] for _ in range(2*n)]\n        for i in range(n):\n            adj[i].append((i+1)%n)\n            adj[(i+1)%n].append(i)\n            adj[i].append(n + i)\n            adj[n + i].append(i)\n            adj[n + i].append(n + (i+k)%n)\n            adj[n + (i+k)%n].append(n + i)\n        r, d = get_radius_and_diam(2*n, adj)\n        rom = fast_roman_subsets(2*n, adj)\n        if r + 1 > rom:\n            print(f\"COUNTEREXAMPLE: Petersen P({n},{k}), r={r}, rom={rom}\")\n            exit(0)\n\n# Grids P_a x P_b\nfor a in range(2, 6):\n    for b in range(2, 6):\n        n = a * b\n        adj = [[] for _ in range(n)]\n        for i in range(a):\n            for j in range(b):\n                u = i * b + j\n                if i + 1 < a:\n                    v = (i+1)*b + j\n                    adj[u].append(v); adj[v].append(u)\n                if j + 1 < b:\n                    v = i*b + (j+1)\n                    adj[u].append(v); adj[v].append(u)\n        r, d = get_radius_and_diam(n, adj)\n        rom = fast_roman_subsets(n, adj)\n        if r + 1 > rom:\n            print(f\"COUNTEREXAMPLE: Grid {a}x{b}, r={r}, rom={rom}\")\n            exit(0)\n\nprint(\"All named graphs satisfy radius + 1 <= roman!\")\n'","Cwd":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Testing named graphs","toolSummary":"Test named graphs for conjecture"}}]}
