om:\n            print(f\"COUNTEREXAMPLE: Petersen P({n},{k}), r={r}, rom={rom}\")\n            exit(0)\n\n# Grids P_a x P_b\nfor a in range(2, 6):\n    for b in range(2, 6):\n        n = a * b\n        adj = [[] for _ in range(n)]\n        for i in range(a):\n            for j in range(b):\n                u = i * b + j\n                if i + 1 < a:\n                    v = (i+1)*b + j\n                    adj[u].append(v); adj[v].append(u)\n                if j + 1 < b:\n                    v = i*b + (j+1)\n                    adj[u].append(v); adj[v].append(u)\n        r, d = get_radius_and_diam(n, adj)\n        rom = fast_roman_subsets(n, adj)\n        if r + 1 > rom:\n            print(f\"COUNTEREXAMPLE: Grid {a}x{b}, r={r}, rom={rom}\")\n            exit(0)\n\nprint(\"All named graphs satisfy radius + 1 <= roman!\")\n'\nTask logs are available at: file:///tmp/agyhome.NWyWnj/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/f458c9cf-488d-4cd8-8365-7c4e4b16e3f9/.system_generated/tasks/task-64.log\nYOU MUST TAKE ONE OF THE FOLLOWING TWO ACTIONS: A) either proceed to other relevant work (if any) or, B) simply update the user with a short message (that you have launched the command and will wait for it to finish) and end the turn.\n DO NOTHING ELSE."}
